// Sparkle.xcconfig
// Sparkle 2 auto-update configuration (TECH-SPEC §10, plan U11).
//
// SU_FEED_URL: PLACEHOLDER — no production web domain exists yet for this
// one-shot build (same situation as AUTH0_DOMAIN in Auth0.xcconfig). Points
// at the apps/web appcast route (a static public/appcast.xml file) under a
// placeholder "whistle.app" domain, matching the sensible-placeholder
// convention used elsewhere in this repo. Replace with the real production
// domain once one exists, then re-run `xcodegen generate`.
//
// SU_PUBLIC_ED_KEY: the PUBLIC half of a Sparkle EdDSA keypair generated
// locally via Sparkle's `generate_keys` tool (see SECRETS.md for exactly
// where the private half lives and how to export it for CI). Safe to
// commit — it's a public key used only to verify appcast signatures.

// NOTE: `//` begins a comment ANYWHERE in an xcconfig line, so a literal
// URL here would silently truncate to `https:`. The empty variable
// substitution `$()` below splits the two slashes without changing the
// resolved value — the standard xcconfig idiom for URLs.
SU_FEED_URL = https:/$()/whistle.app/appcast.xml
SU_PUBLIC_ED_KEY = Y9Xz7q5K5r2Q3o4m/0UPgG9X+oU0zCujfMDbAdzabd4=
